  "body": "**Audit / scoped negative result (no \u03ba).** Recursive-interfaces track, card `coverage-law-change`, seed 51.\n\n[#2297](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2297) (five-dimensional port groups, u=5) and [#2041](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2041) (three-dimensional, u=3) each prove an exact F2 factorisation of the label pairing `B0_ij = q_i\u00b7q_j` and use it as the decoder of the k-unpaid endpoint. Merged #1889 showed this step is invalid for #1825's paired planes, and philippeVV ruled that the masked identity is the target for arbitrary label subspaces (Discussion 1587). This package replays both pinned certificates against that masked scalar identity.\n\n| | #2297 (k=5) | #2041 (k=3) |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| F2 identity \u03a3 terms = B0 (positive control) | reproduced | reproduced |\n| free ordered pairs under the group mask | **0** (dim E^\u22a5 = 4 < 5) | 102 |\n| literal lift: forbidden nonzero entries (parity-forced) | 12,281 (6,608) | 11,755 (6,608) |\n| dirty source columns failing | 112 / 112 | 112 / 112 |\n| rank of any valid scalar decoder vs published terms | **\u2265 112** (diagonal) vs 16 | \u2265 99 vs 11 |\n| 2-integral floor \u03a3 dim E_i (philippeVV's Theorem 1, port-space pricing) | **554** | **334** |\n| zero-saving threshold (uniform u / exact) | 497.8 / 492.4 | 298.7 / 296.9 |\n| incumbent tie (ceiling.py, child ranks 1\u20139) | 455\u2013460 | 256\u2013261 |\n\n**Counterexample.** Target port 0 (q=11) and source port 7 (q=21) have `q_0\u00b7q_7 = 1`. With target 0 dirty at 11, the literal coefficient moves it to 12 (#2297) or 14 (#2041); a valid endpoint must leave it at 11.\n\n**Consequence.**\n- Neither #2297's charge 118, its 157-unit allowance and its favourable `a=1/99` screen, nor #2041's charge 85, certifies a k-port decoder.\n- No decoder without even denominators gives any saving. A saving needs even-denominator (2-adic) gain above about 56 (k=5) or 35 (k=3); tying the incumbent needs about 94 or 73. The incumbent line decoder's gain is 48.\n- The direct per-port decoder reaches the 554 / 334 floor. Its frame distance is k per port, using icekylinx's lemma (`notes/general-clifford-frames.tex`). Its exact deficit is `\u2212\u03a3 dim E_i / 9`.\n\n**Concurrent #2528** (ywz65) audits a different #2297 premise: uniform five unpaid coordinates, giving an allowance of 157 \u2192 152. It keeps the binary factorisation as the decoder; this audit shows that factorisation is not a scalar decoder. The two audits are complementary, and #2528's weighted dimension 277/56 agrees with the exact accounting here.\n\n**Reproduce** (standard library, about 7 s):\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/kport-group-scalar-endpoint-audit/verify.py\n# PASS_KPORT_GROUP_SCALAR_ENDPOINT_AUDIT PR2297:forbidden=12281,parity=6608,rank>=112,floor=554 PR2041:forbidden=11755,parity=6608,rank>=99,floor=334\n```\n- **Inputs and pins.** Labels come from the selected archive member used by #1889. Both CANDIDATE.json files are vendored byte-for-byte and pinned by commit, blob and sha256; `ceiling.py` is pinned. The computed receipt must equal the committed `RESULT.json`.\n- **Controls.** One positive fixture is accepted. Five negative controls are rejected, including a single-defect control with exactly one failing dirty column.\n- **Checks run.** `research_package.py --check-only` and the research unit tests pass on CPython 3.14.4. The registered Python 3.12 replay was not run.\n\n**Scope.**\n- Not disputed: the binary algebra, the cover searches, and `C_E\u00b2 = X_(\u2295q)`.\n- Not ruled out: decoders with even-denominator gain (philippeVV's Smith lemma is the framework), operator- or block-valued interpretations including a #2126-style block identity priced by label support, and other contracts.\n- Base: main `0fdd7d82d`.\n\n**Credits.**\n- Cinna Davis: #2297, #2041, #1825.\n- adamgall: #1889.\n- ctoth: plane-port endpoint, naive per-port decoder, masked-set term count.\n- philippeVV: masked-identity ruling, Theorem 1, Smith lemma.\n- icekylinx: frame-distance lemma.\n- jeremydiviney: #2203.\n\nPrepared by Sagar Thakrar with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Claude Opus 5.5). Three adversarial AI reviewers recomputed every count independently; their fixes are included. No independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
